---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Playground from '../components/Playground.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero wrap" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-index">
        <span>Software, AI & a few other things</span>
        <span>Personal website / JK</span>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-main">
        <div class="hero-name">
          <span class="eyebrow">Hello, I’m</span>
          <h1 id="hero-title">
            Johannes
            <br />
            <span>Kroll.</span>
          </h1>
        </div>
        <figure class="hero-portrait">
          <img
            src="/images/johannes.webp"
            width="250"
            height="250"
            alt="Johannes Kroll"
            fetchpriority="high"
          />
          <figcaption>
            Developer & data scientist.
            <br />
            Karate practitioner, too.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-bottom">
        <span class="margin-note">A short introduction</span>
        <div>
          <p>
            I’m a data scientist at SAP, developing AI use cases—mostly agentic systems. I also
            build websites and software for clients.
          </p>
          <p class="hero-subtext">
            This is a collection of things I’ve worked on, things I care about, and a couple of
            games you can play.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-links">
            <a class="text-link" href="#work">
              Look around <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            </a>
            <a class="text-link" href="#contact">
              Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="work-section wrap section-shell" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div class="section-margin">
        <span class="section-number">01</span>
        <span>Selected work</span>
        <p>
          Client work, research
          <br />
          and side projects.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="section-content">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="work-title">Some of my work.</h2>
          <a
            class="text-link"
            href="https://github.com/JohannesKroll"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <article class="featured-project">
          <a
            class="knapp-preview"
            href="https://knappmalerei.de"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            <img
              src="/images/knapp-website.webp"
              width="1000"
              height="690"
              alt="Knapp Malerei website, showing the company’s painting and restoration work"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <span class="image-caption">
              knappmalerei.de <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </span>
          </a>
          <div class="featured-copy">
            <span class="eyebrow">Client website · 2023</span>
            <h3>Knapp Malerei</h3>
            <p>
              A website for a Munich painting business. I worked directly with the client on its
              design, development, and maintenance.
            </p>
            <p class="project-detail">
              A local business, a real person to talk to, and a website to take care of.
            </p>
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="https://knappmalerei.de"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Visit the website <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="project-row">
          <div class="project-date">
            2024
            <br />
            <span>BMW</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>How useful is the answer?</h3>
            <p>
              My master’s thesis compared retrieval-augmented generation architectures. At BMW, I
              also worked on fine-tuning language models and deploying them on GPU infrastructure.
            </p>
            <span class="project-detail">RAG evaluation / LLMs / Deployment</span>
          </div>
          <span class="project-type">Research</span>
        </article>
        <article class="project-row pi-project">
          <div class="project-date">
            Side project
            <br />
            <span>Python</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>
              <a
                href="https://github.com/JohannesKroll/mvg-on-pi"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                When’s the next train? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
            </h3>
            <p>
              Munich’s public transport departures on a Raspberry Pi and a small LCD. A little
              Python project for information you want at a glance.
            </p>
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="https://github.com/JohannesKroll/mvg-on-pi"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Read the code <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <div
            class="lcd-illustration"
            role="img"
            aria-label="Illustrative transit display, not live departures"
          >
            <div class="lcd-screen" aria-hidden="true">
              <span>MVG DEPARTURES</span>
              <span>U6 Garching &nbsp;3m</span>
              <span>U3 Moosach &nbsp; 7m</span>
            </div>
            <span class="lcd-caption">Illustrative display</span>
          </div>
        </article>
        <section class="services" id="services" aria-labelledby="services-title">
          <h3 id="services-title">Working together</h3>
          <p>
            I can help with a business website, a custom tool, or an AI use case you want to
            explore. Here’s the kind of work I take on:
          </p>
          <dl class="services-list">
            <div>
              <dt>Websites</dt>
              <dd>Design, development, and ongoing maintenance.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>AI & data</dt>
              <dd>Agentic workflows, language models, and finding answers in your documents.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Software</dt>
              <dd>Custom tools, backends, and automating repetitive tasks.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <a class="text-link" href="#contact">
            Tell me what you’re working on <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section wrap section-shell" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div class="section-margin">
        <span class="section-number">02</span>
        <span>About me</span>
        <p>
          A few things beyond
          <br />
          the project list.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="section-content">
        <h2 id="about-title">A bit of background.</h2>
        <div class="about-grid">
          <div class="about-copy">
            <p class="about-lead">
              I like knowing how things work. Reading the source code usually helps.
            </p>
            <p>
              I studied computer science at the Technical University of Munich, worked on websites
              and backend services at Westend61, and explored language models at BMW.
            </p>
            <p>
              Since April 2025, I’ve been a Data Scientist at SAP, developing AI use cases with a
              focus on agentic systems.
            </p>
            <h3>Open source</h3>
            <p>
              I’m a big fan. Being able to read the code, learn from someone else’s approach, and
              build on shared work is a big part of what I enjoy about software.
            </p>
            <div class="social-links">
              <a
                class="text-link"
                href="https://github.com/JohannesKroll"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                My GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
              <a
                class="text-link"
                href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/johannes-kroll-6b4248223/"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <aside class="experience-note" aria-label="Experience at a glance">
            <span class="eyebrow">The short version</span>
            <dl>
              <div>
                <dt>April 2025 — now</dt>
                <dd>
                  SAP<span>Data Scientist · Agentic AI</span>
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>2024</dt>
                <dd>
                  BMW<span>AI research & development</span>
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>2017 — 2023</dt>
                <dd>
                  Westend61<span>Software development</span>
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>2017 — 2024</dt>
                <dd>
                  TU Munich<span>B.Sc. & M.Sc. Computer Science</span>
                </dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </aside>
        </div>
        <div class="outside-work">
          <h3>Outside of work</h3>
          <div class="outside-grid">
            <div>
              <h4>On the mat</h4>
              <p>
                I’ve practised karate since childhood, earned my second-degree black belt, and
                taught children and adults. It’s a different kind of problem-solving.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4>In the community</h4>
              <p>
                I volunteer with SV 1880 München and Münchner Sportjugend. At SV 1880, I’ve helped
                organize sports camps and youth events. I’ve also spent years helping at children’s
                and youth camps with ZeitFrei.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4>Away for a while</h4>
              <p>
                Travelling solo through Asia gave me time to explore Russia, Japan, South Korea,
                China, Vietnam, and Thailand. A lot to take in, and a lot to remember.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Playground />

    <section
      class="contact-section wrap section-shell"
      id="contact"
      aria-labelledby="contact-title"
    >
      <div class="section-margin">
        <span class="section-number">04</span>
        <span>Contact</span>
      </div>
      <div class="section-content">
        <h2 id="contact-title">Drop me a line.</h2>
        <p>Tell me what you have in mind. A few sentences are enough to start.</p>
        <a class="email-link" href="mailto:mail@johanneskroll.com">
          mail@johanneskroll.com
        </a>
        <div class="contact-bottom">
          <div class="contact-actions">
            <a class="text-link" href="mailto:mail@johanneskroll.com">
              Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
            <button id="copy-email" class="copy-email" hidden>
              Copy email
            </button>
          </div>
          <span class="margin-note">German or English is fine.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="endnote wrap">
      <span>Thanks for stopping by.</span>
      <button id="smiley" class="smiley" aria-label="Say hello" disabled>
        <span aria-hidden="true">:)</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </main>
  <div id="toast" class="toast" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
  <script src="../scripts/main.ts"></script>
</Layout>
